"""Mission loader part 1: the mission's loading (game/mission_loader.cpp) against the original's (script/ml_diff.cpp, suite
mission.loader). Run: on script/build_ml.bat, HD2_ML_QUICK=1 (21 of the game's missions and 600 cases); MUT_HARNESS
script, MUT_EXTRA_SRCS original_exe.cpp and ml_calls.s, MUT_LDFLAGS -Wl,--image-base=0x20000000; MUT_PASS
"ml_diff: .*, N checks, 0 failures".

706 mutants, 81 not building; 530 of the 625 building killed at first, 576 after the test was widened (the files'
opens and closes compared, the caches Begin empties given an entry each, the scene's +0x210 and the dummies' boxes
dumped, the lights' attenuation and the lens flares' and projectors' fields, kinds of objects with their own entries
and fresh names, the scene's version first and the lights' entries of its size, cut-short headers in the lists, the
lights, sounds and areas, two parent entries, an empty scene2.bin). The 49 left:
- The port's fix: the shifting textures' name length kept in its buffer (333 cmp, num, arith, and, 334 del, num,
  arith): lengths over 255 are not given (the original writes past its buffer).
- Equivalent: the deleted copy operations (42, 43 del); initial values every path overwrites before reading (62, 268,
  269, 271, 272, 326, 370, 414, 437, 564, 582, 609, 610, 611, 614, 616, 617, 618, 619, 989 num); buffer and array
  sizes (93, 197, 332, 615, 704 num); the chunk's destructor closes the file (66, 68, 150 del) and ascends nothing
  that is read after (260 del); a one-byte file's progress (191 num: no header reads first); the clamp at 0.1 exactly
  (306 cmp: 0.1 either way); counts of 0 at > or >= (572, 584 cmp); a vertex's w and the environment vector's w, not
  read by the engine's calls as logged (575, 1073 num); a short box entry's previous values (853 code, code2, code3,
  code4: every entry full); the lightmaps' handle when the chunk is closed (980 num: never)."""
